prayerTemplate:
PRAYER

In the light of the facts and circumstances stated above, and in view of the urgency of the matter touching upon the personal liberty of the detenu, the Petitioner most respectfully prays that this Hon'ble Court may graciously be pleased to:

a) Issue a writ in the nature of HABEAS CORPUS directing the Respondents to produce the body of the detenu, Shri/Smt. {detenu_name}, before this Hon'ble Court forthwith and to show cause as to under what authority of law he/she is being detained;

b) Upon production, declare the said detention to be illegal and unconstitutional and set the detenu at liberty forthwith;

c) Direct the Respondents to furnish the grounds of detention and the order, if any, by which the detenu has been deprived of his/her liberty;

d) Award appropriate compensation to the detenu for the violation of his/her fundamental rights under Articles 21 and 22 of the Constitution of India;

e) Pending hearing and final disposal of this petition, direct the Respondents to disclose the present whereabouts of the detenu and to permit communication with the next of kin and counsel;

f) Award costs of this petition;

g) Pass any other order(s) as this Hon'ble Court may deem fit and proper in the interest of justice.

And for this act of kindness, the Petitioner shall ever pray.
